or\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Bridge-first user responses still create duplicate canonical archive entries\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"`ProcessHistoryCompatService` derives bridged `user_message` keys from `historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:61-68`), while `ProcessResponseService` archives the same accepted response under `response:${clientRequestId}` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:153-168`). `ArchiveFinalizationService` only short-circuits when an existing row with the same `sourceObjectId` is already present (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:70-79`), so the opposite order still duplicates. I reproduced this with `corepack pnpm exec tsx` by calling `submitProcessResponse()` -> `appendFromProcessHistoryItem()` -> `respond()`; the archive then contained two `user_message` rows for the same `sourceObjectId`: `response:process-archive-finalization:history-response-1` and `response:req-archive-4`.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\\\",\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\\\",\\\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\\\",\\\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"AC-2.3\\\",\\\"TC-2.3b\\\",\\\"DoD-compatibility-mapping\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"quick-fix\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-green-verify-format-failure\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Story gate currently fails at format check\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` exited 1 in `format:check` because Biome would reformat the constructor type wrapping in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:15-17`. The story gate therefore does not pass in the current workspace.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"StoryGate\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"quick-fix\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-live-archive-separation-proof-missing\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Required live/archive separation test coverage is still missing\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Story 2's Definition of Done and test plan require proof that live history upserts keep updating current state without creating archive rows. Repo search found no archive assertions in the designated live-surface tests: `rg -n \\\\\\\"archive|appendArchive|ArchiveFinalization\\\\\\\" tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts apps/platform/server/services/processes/live/process-live-normalizer.ts apps/platform/client/app/process-live.ts` returned no matches, and the added focused tests only cover `tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts` plus archive seed mapping.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts\\\",\\\"tests/service/server/process-live-updates.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"DoD-live-archive-separation\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"quick-fix\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true}],\\\"openFindings\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-user-message-bridge-key-mismatch\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"major\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Bridge-first user responses still create duplicate canonical archive entries\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"`ProcessHistoryCompatService` derives bridged `user_message` keys from `historyItemId` (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts:61-68`), while `ProcessResponseService` archives the same accepted response under `response:${clientRequestId}` (`apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:153-168`). `ArchiveFinalizationService` only short-circuits when an existing row with the same `sourceObjectId` is already present (`apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:70-79`), so the opposite order still duplicates. I reproduced this with `corepack pnpm exec tsx` by calling `submitProcessResponse()` -> `appendFromProcessHistoryItem()` -> `respond()`; the archive then contained two `user_message` rows for the same `sourceObjectId`: `response:process-archive-finalization:history-response-1` and `response:req-archive-4`.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/process-history-compat.service.ts\\\",\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\\\",\\\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts\\\",\\\"tests/service/server/archive-finalization.test.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"AC-2.3\\\",\\\"TC-2.3b\\\",\\\"DoD-compatibility-mapping\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"quick-fix\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-green-verify-format-failure\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Story gate currently fails at format check\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"`corepack pnpm run green-verify` exited 1 in `format:check` because Biome would reformat the constructor type wrapping in `apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts:15-17`. The story gate therefore does not pass in the current workspace.\\\",\\\"affectedFiles\\\":[\\\"apps/platform/server/services/archive/archive-finalization.service.ts\\\"],\\\"requirementIds\\\":[\\\"StoryGate\\\"],\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\":\\\"quick-fix\\\",\\\"blocking\\\":true},{\\\"id\\\":\\\"story2-live-archive-separation-proof-missing\\\",\\\"severity\\\":\\\"minor\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"Required live/archive separation test coverage is still missing\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Story 2's Definition of Done and test plan require proof that live history upserts keep updating current state without creating archive rows. Repo search found no archive assertions in the designated live-surface tests: `rg -n \\\\\\\"archive|appendArchive|Arch